essarily putting the  technical words to it bam bam  communication among different mediums  finds a way we guess it makes sense they  communicate in a similar way they both  work with bodies after all just in  different contexts musical theater has  this incredible tradition of telling  story through song  you can do a lot apparently  you can really feel the larger than life  characters and the joy just flowing out  of the dancers in this piece cartoons  often do things like defy the laws of  gravity so we were a bit surprised to  see just how well they captured the  character performance  just an incredible feeling you know  incredible sense of  accomplishment whoever's idea it was to  hire lin-manuel miranda is a genius  the music legend most notably known for  the broadway musical hamilton before  this was brought on board to write the  music for the movie  he was one of the crew who traveled to  colombia to immerse himself in the  culture and get acquainted with the very  specific sound of the music it isn't  common for a disney movie to be written  in 3-4 time miranda said but this movie  was an exception given that time  signature is incredibly important to  colombian rhythm working on a song with  12 very original and different actors it  inspired miranda to find the pulse of  each character and connect them with  different kinds of colombian music  miranda also recorded himself singing  every character's part for we don't talk  about bruno and probably all of the  other music too he finds it the easiest  way to get his intention across here's  hoping disney one day releases a full  album that would be amazing i just said  for the next one can i just please be  there from the beginning i want to be as  involved as i can be this is probably  the biggest project ever done from home  all of the acting and all of the  coaching actually happened over zoom and  the actors worked out of their own home  studios stephanie beatrice who plays  mirabelle admitted that she didn't find  the process all that strange because  voice acting is usually pretty isolated  anyways i'm part of the amazing madrid  she's actually found herself closer to  the director because he was right there  on zoom rather than behind a glass panel  lin-manuel was a huge cheerleader for  the actors he's also incredibly patient  which is good for nervous singers it was  actually adasa's idea to make dolores  sing her lines an octave lower just  above a whisper in the song we don't  talk about bruno that's just one element  that all of that character development  brought to the table  personalization i just felt like a tiger  like i seized the moment  imagine how much has to be in place  before the animators can even start  it's always so cool to look back at the  concept art because it ranges so wildly  in character design and costume you can  see how the early art informs the final  choices but also why some things were  cut like mirabelle was designed to be  wearing heels at one point just imagine  how much that would affect her movement  in the movie taking out those high heels  also would have knocked her down a peg  as high heels can present as very  confident something that she's not from  the start  hopefully bring my best to  mirabelle  casa casa madrigo casita for short the  one limitation the crew were working  with designing the gorgeous madrigal  home was that they wanted the house to  be alive but they didn't want it to bend  to the elements in order to move  that choice really made this living  house distinct from other living houses  and yes there are more remember a movie  called monster house that's just the  first to come to mind the house  expresses most of its personality  through its tile flipping and window  panes they went through a lot of concept  art to get the house just right which is  fair it's as much a character as the  rest of the family the whole movie could  essentially take place in this house but  it was limitless of what it 